- powershell -File scripts/smoke-windows.ps1 -UpstreamWaitSeconds 300 -CDPMode all: exit 1; listeners, attach, WMPF upstream, and Runtime exception response succeeded, then the matrix rejected optional StackTrace.description.

# Skipped checks

The live matrix stopped at the Runtime exception assertion. Debugger, Page, DOM, Network, Console, Performance, input interaction, connected graceful shutdown, target survival, and final success marker were not reached in this run.

# Spec consistency

The implementation scope is complete and deterministic checks match the public SDK specification. The live response contained exceptionDetails.text, exception.description, and stackTrace.callFrames. CDP defines StackTrace.description as optional, so the smoke assertion is stricter than the protocol and must be corrected in Build.

# Known limitations and risks

Live production parity remains unverified until the corrected matrix completes every domain, reconnect, interaction, shutdown, target-survival, and port-rebind check in one run.

# Conclusion

Verify fails for a concrete smoke-client validation bug found by the real WMPF target. Return to Build, validate standard stackTrace.callFrames, update fixtures, refreeze scope, and rerun all evidence.
